  <h2 id="behaviour">Behaviour</h2>
  <p>Load <code>dawn-and-dusk.js</code> and add <code>data-dd-data-table</code> to the root. Everything is delegated, so rows added later just work.</p>
  <ClassTable head={['Attribute / element', 'Behaviour']} rows={[
    ['th[aria-sort] .dd-data-table__sort', 'Click cycles <code>none → ascending → descending → none</code> and sorts the rows by each cell’s <code>data-value</code>, else its text. Two values compare as numbers when both are fully numeric (<code>1,240</code>, <code>0.5%</code>, <code>-3</code>), as times when both are ISO dates (<code>2026-10-30</code>, <code>2026-10-30T09:41</code>), else as text with numbers in order (<code>v2</code> before <code>v10</code>). In an <code>.is-num</code> column, “84 ms” still reads as 84 and a dash counts as blank. Blanks sort last; groups and detail rows stay together.'],
    ['thead .dd-data-table__check', 'Selects or clears every visible row; shows indeterminate when some are selected. Rows whose box is <code>disabled</code> are skipped and don’t count toward its state.'],
    ['tbody .dd-data-table__check', 'Selects the row (<code>.is-selected</code>). Shift-click selects a range (skipping disabled boxes). A <code>disabled</code> box is never changed by the table — select all, ranges and Clear leave it as it is.'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-selected]', 'Receives the selected count. <code>.dd-data-table__bulk</code> is shown while it is above zero; if it hides with focus inside (a bulk action removed the rows), focus moves to the select-all box.'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-clear]', 'Clears the selection.'],
    ['.dd-data-table__expand', 'Toggles <code>aria-expanded</code> and the <code>hidden</code> detail row named by <code>aria-controls</code>.'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-search]', 'Filters rows by their text as you type.'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-filter="col=value"]', 'Toggle chip (<code>aria-pressed</code>) or checkbox (e.g. in a <code>__menu</code>). Matches cells with <code>data-col="col"</code> by <code>data-value</code> or text. Same column = any, different columns = all.'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-filter-label="col"]', 'Shows <code>all</code>, the one value or “2 selected” for that column, and marks its chip <code>.is-active</code>.'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-removable]', 'On a filter chip: it disappears once cleared (focus moves to the search).'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-count="noun"]', 'Shows “12 services”, or “3 of 12 services” while filtered.'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-query]', 'Receives the quoted search text in the empty state.'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-reset]', 'Clears search and chips, and returns focus to the search.'],
    ['[data-dd-pagination] inside the root', 'Pages the matching rows in the browser (see <a href="pagination">pagination</a>): <code>data-total</code> is kept in step, the page-size select and arrows move through the rows. Filtering goes back to page 1; sorting keeps the page.'],
    ['[data-dd-data-table-column="col"]', 'Checkbox that shows / hides the column whose header has <code>data-col="col"</code>.'],
    ['Rows added or removed', 'Picked up on their own (count, filters, empty row, pages and selection refresh on the next frame); <code>dd.dataTable.refresh(root)</code> does it by hand.'],
    ['Focus on removed rows', 'When the row holding focus is removed (a ⋯ menu’s Remove, a bulk action, a framework re-render), focus moves to the first control of the next shown row, else the previous one, else the select-all box, else the scroll region. A row that is only moved keeps its focus. Try it: a row’s ⋯ → Remove from fleet.'],
    ['Keyboard', 'Every control is a native button, checkbox or input, so <kbd>Tab</kbd>, <kbd>Enter</kbd> and <kbd>Space</kbd> work throughout. The scroll region is focusable, so arrow keys scroll it. <kbd>Esc</kbd> closes a column or filter menu and returns focus to its button; a click outside closes it too.'],
    ['Events', '<code>dd:sort</code> <code>{ column, direction, index }</code> after a header sorts; <code>dd:selectionchange</code> <code>{ count, rows }</code> after the selection changes; <code>dd:pagechange</code> (from the pager) <code>{ page, pages, pageSize, total, from, to }</code>. All bubble from the root, so a server-backed table can listen and fetch.'],
  ]} />

  <script is:inline>
    // Docs only: the flagship's row menu can remove its row (the menu knows which row through menu.ddTrigger).
    document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      if (!e.target.closest('#dt-row-menu [data-dt-remove]')) return;
      const row = document.getElementById('dt-row-menu').ddTrigger?.closest('tr');
      if (!row) return;
      const name = row.querySelector('[data-col="service"] a')?.textContent;
      document.getElementById(row.querySelector('.dd-data-table__expand')?.getAttribute('aria-controls'))?.remove();
      row.remove();
      window.dd?.toast?.({ title: `${name} removed`, description: 'Focus moved to the next row.' });
    });
  </script>

  <h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
  <Guides
    do={['Freeze the column that names the row so it stays in view while scrolling sideways.', 'Right-align figures, use mono and keep one unit per column.', 'Show the selected count and only the bulk actions that apply to it.', 'Keep sorting, filtering and selection state in the URL in real apps.']}
    dont={['Don’t wrap cells; truncate and show the rest in the expanded row.', 'Don’t hide the header or the count while filtering.', 'Don’t paint whole rows red; mark the cell and the status.', 'Don’t put primary buttons inside rows. Use a ghost “more” menu.']}
  />
